    "why": "Bold wall strokes (James Coke style, as Esqueleto). Thin walls the scan breaks into pieces are joined across 5 px gaps (weakBridgePx) and kept from 40 px (weakMinExtentPx), and walls drawn with a 2 px pen from 25 px (thinWallMinExtentPx): passages like Aluxe's Key had lost a wall or both. Labels OCR misses or reads too poorly, the p. depth labels and KLS are boxed (labelBoxes, letters only) and anchor their leaders, which go - their straight run from the label (leaderStraightPx 10, as leaders curve gently here), starting within 35 px of it (leaderReachPx) and 60 px of a cross-section (sectionReachPx): further, thin walls ending near a label passed for leaders. Leaders still missed, and the Coba road's dashed line, are erased by hand. Floor reliefs (outlines and lines with ticks: rings around pits and ledges along the walls) are found as rows of ticks agreeing with their neighbours (localAlignment) and redrawn - a ring closed, a ledge along a wall as its ticks only, the wall kept (onWalls). Boulders drawn filled and standing apart (small, round, mostly solid) aren't walls (dropSolidPx), and narrow passages whose walls the boulders join are erased and their walls drawn by hand (wallLines), as is Aluxe's Key's south wall, broken on the scan.",
